INTRODUCTION
The rapid growth of retail participation in the Indian stock market has led to an increase in the number of individual investors. However, most retail investors lack the tools and expertise required to interpret financial data effectively.
While platforms like Economic Times Markets provide extensive market data, the complexity of this data makes it difficult for beginners to derive actionable insights.
This project aims to bridge this gap by developing an AI-powered system that simplifies financial data and provides personalized investment insights.


Problem Statement
India has 14 crore+ demat accounts, but most retail investors are flying blind - reacting to tips, missing filings, unable to read technicals, and managing mutual fund portfolios on gut feel. ET Markets has the data. Build the intelligence layer that turns data into actionable, money-making decisions. 


Functional Requirements
The system provides the following functionalities:
User registration and profile management
Input of investor preferences (risk, budget, duration)
Retrieval of stock market data
Analysis of stock trends and performance
AI-based recommendation generation
Visualization of stock trends and insights
Display of simplified investment suggestions 


Non-Functional Requirements
Performance: System should respond quickly to user queries
Usability: Interface should be simple and beginner-friendly
Security: User data must be protected
Reliability: System should provide consistent results
Scalability: Should support multiple users simultaneously
Maintainability: Code should be modular and easy to update


System Architecture
The system follows a modular architecture:
Frontend: User interface for interaction
Backend: Handles logic and processing
Intelligence Engine: Generates insights
Data Source: Stock APIs or datasets
FLOW : User → Frontend → Backend → Intelligence Engine → Data → Output


